From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:11:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: fast scroller follows scroll without restarting
 per frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VerticalMasonryFastScroller restarted its follow effect on every change
of scroll offset, max scroll, and canScrollForward. A fling writes the
offset on each frame, so that coroutine was cancelled and started again
for every one of them and the shelf stuttered.

One effect now collects a snapshotFlow of those three values. It still
returns without moving the thumb while the thumb is dragged. The effect
is keyed on the track height and top padding, which change with the
layout rather than with each frame, so a resize still picks up the new
track.

The list scroller assigns the thumb during composition. The grid
scroller's LaunchedEffect(firstVisibleItemScrollOffset) is upstream and
closes over row estimates recomputed in composition, so it is left as
it is.

与 anikku-harmony 0037 同源。
---
 .../core/components/VerticalFastScroller.kt   | 31 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/presentation-core/src/main/java/tachiyomi/presentation/core/components/VerticalFastScroller.kt b/presentation-core/src/main/java/tachiyomi/presentation/core/components/VerticalFastScroller.kt
index 616fa2b..7f7c600 100644
--- a/presentation-core/src/main/java/tachiyomi/presentation/core/components/VerticalFastScroller.kt
+++ b/presentation-core/src/main/java/tachiyomi/presentation/core/components/VerticalFastScroller.kt
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ import kotlinx.coroutines.channels.BufferOverflow
 import kotlinx.coroutines.coroutineScope
 import kotlinx.coroutines.delay
 import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.MutableSharedFlow
+import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.collect
 import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.collectLatest
 import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.first
 import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.sample
@@ -521,19 +522,25 @@ fun VerticalMasonryFastScroller(
             }
 
             val lastScrollOffset = remember { MutableData(Float.NaN) }
-            LaunchedEffect(state.scrollOffset, state.maxScroll, state.canScrollForward) {
-                if (isThumbDragged) return@LaunchedEffect
-                val proportion = if (!state.canScrollForward) {
-                    1f
-                } else {
-                    (state.scrollOffset / state.maxScroll).coerceIn(0f, 1f)
-                }
-                val target = trackHeightPx * proportion + thumbTopPadding
-                if (state.scrollOffset != lastScrollOffset.value) {
-                    lastScrollOffset.value = state.scrollOffset
-                    scrolled.tryEmit(Unit)
+            // Harmony: a fling moves the offset every frame, and restarting this effect
+            // stalled the shelf. The collector stays up and still skips a grabbed thumb.
+            LaunchedEffect(trackHeightPx, thumbTopPadding) {
+                snapshotFlow {
+                    Triple(state.scrollOffset, state.maxScroll, state.canScrollForward)
+                }.collect { (scrollOffset, maxScroll, canScrollForward) ->
+                    if (isThumbDraggedState.value) return@collect
+                    val proportion = if (!canScrollForward) {
+                        1f
+                    } else {
+                        (scrollOffset / maxScroll).coerceIn(0f, 1f)
+                    }
+                    val target = trackHeightPx * proportion + thumbTopPadding
+                    if (scrollOffset != lastScrollOffset.value) {
+                        lastScrollOffset.value = scrollOffset
+                        scrolled.tryEmit(Unit)
+                    }
+                    thumbOffsetY = target
                 }
-                thumbOffsetY = target
             }
 
             val alpha = remember { Animatable(0f) }
